{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:508a709f60621acb","name":"Amphistaff","source":{"id":"source:reference-508a709f60621acb","title":"Amphistaff","revision":15818,"timestamp":"2024-08-18T00:53:14Z","sha256":"7cce625875b6ea6d563970aed76a5428e472dd048102df72b6ca78f1a5cc67f3","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=15818","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Amphistaff&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-508a709f60621acb","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Core Rulebook"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Core_Rulebook"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["An Amphistaff is a serpentine creature genetically engineered by the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Yuuzhan Vong"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Yuuzhan_Vong","referenceId":"reference:93079e2f7d73d480"}," to serve as a weapon. The Amphistaff can become as rigid as stone or as flexible as rope, and it can contract the muscles around its head and tail to form razor-sharp edges. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Yuuzhan Vong"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Yuuzhan_Vong","referenceId":"reference:93079e2f7d73d480"}," treat the Amphistaff as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Simple Weapon"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Simple_Weapon"},", rather than an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Exotic Weapon"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Exotic_Weapon"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Amphistaff has three distinct weapon forms: Quarterstaff, Spear, and Whip. Switching from one Weapon Form to is a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Swift Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swift_Action"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Quarterstaff Form"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["A rigid Amphistaff has all the qualities of a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Quarterstaff"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Quarterstaff","referenceId":"reference:7088a9561b9e8818"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Damage:"]}," 1d6/1d6\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Stun"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Stun"}," Setting:"]}," NO\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Type:"]}," Bludgeoning\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Spear Form"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["A rigid Amphistaff can be wielded or thrown as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Spear"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Spear","referenceId":"reference:c71c66ea7e4c65d6"},". The Spear's head is poisonous: if the target takes damage, and the attack roll equals or exceeds its ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},", the target moves -1 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Persistent"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Persistent"}," step on the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Condition Track"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Condition_Track"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Damage:"]}," 1d8\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Stun"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Stun"}," Setting:"]}," NO\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Type:"]}," Piercing\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Special:"]}," Amphistaffs can be ",{"tag":"a","children":["Thrown"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Thrown"}," in Spear Form\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Whip Form"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["A flexible Amphistaff has a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reach"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reach"}," of 2 squares. The Whip's tail deals 1d4 points of Piercing damage (plus the wielder's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Strength"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Strength"}," modifier) and is poisonous: If the target takes damage, and the attack roll equals or exceeds its ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},", the target moves -1 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Persistent"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Persistent"}," step on the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Condition Track"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Condition_Track"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Instead of dealing damage with the Whip, the wielder may use it to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Pin"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pin","referenceId":"reference:ff1cee74414621d8"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Trip"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Trip","referenceId":"reference:bd13d5a0906be48e"}," the target as though they were using the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Pin"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pin","referenceId":"reference:ff1cee74414621d8"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Trip"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Trip","referenceId":"reference:bd13d5a0906be48e"}," feats. The wielder must be proficient with the Amphistaff, but doesn't need to have the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Pin"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pin","referenceId":"reference:ff1cee74414621d8"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Trip"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Trip","referenceId":"reference:bd13d5a0906be48e"}," feats, to use this weapon feature.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Damage:"]}," 1d4\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Stun"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Stun"}," Setting:"]}," NO\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Type:"]}," Piercing\n"]},"\n","\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Weapon Type:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Exotic Weapons (Melee)"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Exotic_Weapons_(Melee)","referenceId":"reference:e0213365f7fdde76"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Size:"]}," Large\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Weight:"]}," 2 Kilograms\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Availability:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rare"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rare"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Special:"]}," An Amphistaff, in any Form,  may be coaxed by its wielder to spit venom up to 10 squares away (as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Standard Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Standard_Action"},"). If this ranged attack hits both the target's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},", the target moves -1 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Persistent"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Persistent"}," step on the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Condition Track"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Condition_Track"},". An Amphistaff can only spit venom once every 24 standard hours.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
